## Vendored marketplace content

These are not dependencies — they are third-party source files copied into the
repository and shipped inside the app, so their notices are reproduced here in
full rather than pointed at.

### Skills for Real Engineers — https://github.com/mattpocock/skills

MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock.

Twenty-six skills from that repository's `skills/engineering`,
`skills/productivity` and `skills/misc` directories are vendored under
`resources/marketplace/packages/`, one directory per marketplace package, and
are listed in the catalog with `"publisher": "Matt Pocock"`. Each `SKILL.md`
carries `license: MIT` in its frontmatter so the licence travels with the file
once a user installs it.

The copies are upstream's text, with two deliberate edits recorded here:

- Upstream's `code-review` ships as `review-changes`, because the name is
  already taken by the skill nested in Agent V's own `quality` plugin and the
  loader resolves skills by name. The three sibling skills that referred to it
  (`ask-matt`, `implement`, `tdd`) were retargeted to match.
- `agents/openai.yaml`, per-skill display metadata for a different harness, is
  not copied.

